def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement51 : String := "The Funder Registry needs no membership. It is an open registry of persistent identifiers for grant-giving organisations, and the funding metadata is deposited with the work."
def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement52 : String := "ROR needs no membership. It is an open registry of persistent identifiers for research organisations. Crossref co-founded it and runs it with DataCite and the California Digital Library. ROR identifiers in affiliation metadata are tracked in the participation report."
def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement53 : String := "Similarity Check is for members. Crossref provides it and iThenticate powers it, so an editor can compare a submission for overlap."
def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement54 : String := "Crossmark is for members. The button on a landing page shows the current status of an item, including corrections, retractions and updates."
def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement55 : String := "The public REST API is https://api.crossref.org and returns JSON. No signup is required. Members deposit the metadata. Trusted sources such as Retraction Watch add to it. Records can carry funding, licence, updates, ORCID, ROR and abstracts. Almost none of the metadata is under copyright. Some abstracts may be. Swagger is at https://api.crossref.org/.\nidea: /works lists the content items registered with Crossref.\nidea: /journals lists journals and the works of an ISSN.\nidea: /members lists the organisations that registered metadata.\nidea: /prefixes names the steward of a DOI prefix and its works.\nidea: /funders lists the Open Funder Registry and the works of a funder.\nidea: /types lists work types such as journal-article, monograph and grant.\nidea: /licenses lists the licences used by registered content.\nidea: /works/{doi}/agency names the registration agency of a DOI."
def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement56 : String := "The public pool needs no signup: 5 single-record requests per second and concurrency 1. The polite pool is 10 per second and concurrency 3 and asks for a contact, which is not stored here. A list of records is slower: 1 per second on the public pool and 3 on the polite pool. Metadata Plus is 150 per second and names no concurrency cap. The response headers x-rate-limit-limit, x-rate-limit-interval and x-rate-limit-type say which limit applied. A 429 means wait and send more slowly."
def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement57 : String := "The CERN Open Data portal is the access point to preserved output of research at CERN, with the software and documentation needed to understand and analyse it. The products are shared under open licences and issued with a DOI so they can be cited."
def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement58 : String := "LHC data is described in four levels. The portal focuses on levels 2 and 3, and the collaborations may add small samples of level 4.\nidea: Level 1 adds figures and tables to published results.\nidea: Level 2 is simplified data for outreach and training.\nidea: Level 3 is reconstructed and simulated data with analysis software.\nidea: Level 4 is raw data with reconstruction and simulation software."
def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement59 : String := "The four LHC experiments publish data after an embargo stated in their own policies. The portal endorses the FORCE 11 Joint Declaration of Data Citation Principles. Every dataset has a citation recommendation and a BibTeX record so a reuse can be cited and INSPIRE can track it."
