def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement66 : String := "The CERN openlab talk of 8 August 2023 presents OligoArchive, a storage stack that writes digital data onto synthetic DNA. The pipeline randomizes the bits, adds LDPC error control, then indexes them before synthesis. Nothing is fetched here.\nidea: The DNA4DNA pilot stored a 14 MB SIARD archive in 261336 oligos of 280 nucleotides and reported full recovery.\nidea: Each oligo holds a few hundred nucleotides, and the ordering is written into the sequence because a DNA molecule has no address.\n idea: Homopolymers and the balance of G and C constrain which sequences the archive will store."
def quantumProcessingIdeas_statement67 : String := "OligoArchive encodes each attribute with a SHA-3 checksum and interleaves the two, so the avalanche of SHA-3 makes similar values into different DNA sequences. SHA-3 is FIPS 202: SHA3-256 has capacity 512 and rate 1088, and SHA3-512 has capacity 1024 and rate 576, on the 1600-bit state. CERN hosts the paper. NIST wrote the hash. Nothing is fetched here.\nidea: A fixed-length hash of the table name and of the record id is encoded two bits to one nucleotide.\n idea: Two bits a nucleotide is the same rate as two bases a nibble.\n  idea: Thirty-two hex digits hold 64 bases.\n   idea: A, C, G and T are the digits 0, 1, 2 and 3, and the 64 bases read back one for one.\n    idea: AC encodes as 1 and GT encodes as 11, which is hex 1b.\n     idea: One divided by 4 is 0 with remainder 1, so hex 1 reads back as AC, and 11 divided by 4 is 2 with remainder 3, so it reads back as GT.\nidea: Reed-Solomon correction is written between the fields and the attribute value.\nidea: pg_oligo_dump archived 12 KB of TPC-H, 44 records, as oligos of 138 nucleotides.\n idea: Of the 138 nucleotides, 91 hold the data and the two primers use 26 and 21.\n  idea: The sequenced pool held 1941 oligos, and schema information restored the original database.\n   idea: Parity and decode validation retained 1281 reads, and those reads cover the original 404 oligos.\n    idea: The pair filter left 43925 reads, and the parity filter left 23409.\n     idea: The identifier filter left 19 million reads for the Postgres oligos, 65 million for the images, and 3 million with an invalid file id."
